 Spinners animate in the client only while one is visible. Every spinner steps together each 100 ms, and only the changed cells are repainted. `herdr config check` reports an entry with a missing or wrong-width icon, an empty or wrong-width frame, or a malformed color, and that state falls back to its preset glyph and theme color. Overrides apply wherever status icons appear, including the mobile layout. Agent toasts use them too: a needs-attention toast shows the `blocked` icon and a finished toast the `done` icon, while unset states keep the stock toast dot. Overrides color the icon only; style the `state_text` sidebar token separately.
 
+Sprites are small animations for Agent rows, drawn by a `sprite:<name>` token. Define each under `[ui.sprites.<name>]` with frames per state:
+
+```toml
+[ui.sprites.crab]
+interval_ms = 160
+color = "#ff9da4"
+working = ["⡳⡽⢯⢞⠀⠀", "⠘⡮⣿⢵⠃⠀", "⠀⡳⡽⢯⢞⠀"]
+idle = ["⠀⡳⡽⢯⢞⠀"]
+
+[ui.sidebar.agents.rows_by_agent]
+claude = [["sprite:crab", "agent"], ["state_text"]]
+```
+
+- `blocked`, `working`, `done`, `idle`, `unknown` — the frames for that state. Every frame of a sprite, across all states, has the same width of 1–12 cells, so the row doesn't shift as it animates. A state without frames uses `idle`'s; with neither, the token leaves the row.
+- `interval_ms` — milliseconds per frame, 50–5000. Defaults to 250.
+- `color` — `#RGB` or `#RRGGBB`. Defaults to the row's status icon color, so a sprite follows the state colors.
+- `colors` — per-state colors that override `color`, such as `colors = { blocked = "#f55", done = "#a6e3a1" }`. A token `fg` overrides all of them.
+
+Braille characters make good pixel art: each cell is a 2×4 dot grid. Sprites share the spinner clock: they animate only while visible, a one-frame state never repaints, and only changed cells are redrawn. `sprite:` tokens take fixed styles but no `rules`, and work in Agent rows and `rows_by_agent`, not Space rows. `herdr config check` reports an invalid name, an empty or wrong-width frame, frames of different widths, an out-of-range interval, or a malformed `color` or `colors` entry, and that sprite's tokens are left out.
+
